 "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
 "title": "Ashes",
 "dates": "Wednesday, February 17 – Saturday, February 20, 2010",
 "logline": "Ash Wednesday in Mid-City and the long way home: ashes from the man who poured the water, a porch full of Broussards with questions nobody answers, thirty-five hours in a van where nobody touches anybody, a pack nobody opens — and on Saturday, a priest who used to be a doctor.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the levee, Lena: “And till then, nothing. Nothing either one of us would have to explain. Not to them. Not to Mama. Not in a confessional.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the top of the steps, You: “Sunday.” — Lena: “Sunday,” … “And then Tuesday.”",
   "if": "s2e16_after==\"sincerity\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the top of the steps, You: “Lent’s in eighteen minutes.” — Lena: “Then walk me to it, Youngstown.”",
   "if": "s2e16_after==\"wit\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the top of the steps, Lena: “Sunday. I told you. After Mass. To his face, when we’re both back.”",
   "if": "s2e16_after!=\"sincerity\" && s2e16_after!=\"wit\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Lena: “What are you giving up?” … “For Lent.” — You: “Cigarettes.” — Lena: “…I know.” … — You: “You?” — Lena: “Something Laney’s going to take personally.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "In the darkroom, Skye: “When you come back,” … “Whatever you’ve got. Whatever happens down there — the Saints, Mardi Gras, a float falls on you. You tell me. To my face.”",
   "if": "promised_skye_truth"
  },
  {
   "text": "Behind the screen, Father Osei: “You think she’s the answer.” … “To what question?”"
  },
  {
   "text": "A text from Gina at one in the morning: “nonna says maria caterina is a good name for a wife”"
  }
 ],
